From b7238ca06636cde9b5b7c4d2eac76236ba3e7244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:17:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.9.1: Device Identity Manager (Rung B - unified
 long-term storage)

Storage tab (System Log group) selecting a durable location (RAM/JFFS/USB
dot-dir) for opt-in history datasets; no new store, no new daemon.

- defaults.c: reaper_store (ram|jffs|usb) + reaper_store_ds (dev traf watch chq slog)
- web.c do_reaper_dev_cgi: store_status/store_set actions, rdev_store_base()
  resolver (mirrors the shell one), page-action audit ring, rtraf_path fold-in
- rc/rwatch.c: history writer rides the watchdog tick (presence deltas, rchqd
  snapshot, syslog mirror), resolver-aware rwatch DUMPROOT (/jffs fallback)
- www/Reaper_Storage.asp: new native page (location chips + per-dataset toggles
  + health line + Samba-visibility note), RDST_* tokens, registered native+langcheck
- Reaper_Traffic.asp storage select demoted to read-only + link (single writable UI)
- Reaper_Devices.asp: storage status link; menuTree System Log tab
- RDST_00..42 English-seeded into all 25 dicts (lockstep)
